{
  "id": "T-1653",
  "created_at": 1791225114.8516119,
  "parent": "T-1651",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: orchestrator new <path>: create or adopt an empty folder as a git repo, scaffold it with install(), one commit, launch nothing",
  "spec": "Add a CLI subcommand `orchestrator new <path>` that turns a new or empty folder into a scaffolded orchestrator repo,\nso the Planner never needs mkdir or git init (planner-mode.sh blocks both, for subagents too). It launches nothing.\n\nNew module orchestrator/new_project.py with `create(path) -> list[str]` (report lines) and a small wiring in\norchestrator/cli.py next to the \"install\" and \"goal\" parsers (cli.py:197, 236-238, 654-660).\n\nBehaviour of create(path):\n1. p = Path(path).expanduser(); resolve the parent with os.path.realpath. The parent must exist and be a directory,\n   else raise NewProjectError(\"parent does not exist: ...\").\n2. Accept p only if one of these holds, else raise NewProjectError with the reason and change nothing:\n   a. p does not exist;\n   b. p is an empty directory;\n   c. p is a git toplevel (git rev-parse --show-toplevel equals p) with no commits (git rev-parse --verify HEAD fails)\n      and nothing in it except .git.\n   Anything else (non-empty folder, repo with commits, a file, a path inside another repo's working tree that is not its\n   own toplevel) is refused.\n3. Create the directory (case a), run `git init -b main` (cases a and b), then call the existing\n   orchestrator.install.install(str(p)) and keep its report lines.\n4. git add -A and commit with message\n     \"orchestrator: scaffold (new project)\\n\\nWhat: orchestrator install scaffold for a new project.\\nWhy: the Planner starts new projects through `orchestrator new`.\\nRevert: delete the folder; nothing else depends on it yet.\"\n   using the user's git identity (no -c overrides in production code). If the commit fails, raise NewProjectError\n   with git's stderr (files stay; the message says so).\n5. No remote, no push, no network, no Planner or daemon launch, no write outside p.\n6. Return report lines: \"created <p>\" (or \"used existing <p>\"), \"git init -b main\" when run, install's lines, and\n   \"commit <short sha>\".\n\ncli.py: `new = sub.add_parser(\"new\"); new.add_argument(\"path\")`; on NewProjectError print \"new: <reason>\" to stderr and\nexit 2; on success print the report lines, then\n  Next: ORCH_ROOT=<p> uv run orchestrator daemon   (and the goal start line as an alternative)\n\nTests: new file tests/test_new_project.py, unittest style like tests/test_goals.py (read it for the temp-repo helpers and\nhow install() is exercised; set GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL in os.environ for the test process\nonly, and commit.gpgsign=false via GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY/VALUE env). Named tests:\n- test_new_creates_repo_with_scaffold_commit: missing path -> dir exists, branch main, exactly one commit with the\n  message subject above, .orchestrator/pool.toml present, working tree clean.\n- test_new_accepts_empty_dir\n- test_new_accepts_empty_initialised_repo (git init done beforehand, no commits)\n- test_new_refuses_non_empty_dir (one file inside -> NewProjectError, folder unchanged)\n- test_new_refuses_repo_with_commits\n- test_new_refuses_missing_parent\n- test_new_launches_nothing: patch orchestrator.goals.start and subprocess.Popen to fail if called; create() still succeeds\n- test_cli_new_exit_codes: main([\"new\", <bad path>]) exits 2 with \"new:\" on stderr; a good path exits 0 and prints \"Next:\"\n\nRun: uv run python -m pytest -q tests/test_new_project.py tests/test_goals.py (or unittest if pytest is absent).\nCommit on the task branch.\n",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1652"
  ],
